faces.description:
The hub recognises people and gives each a number, but will not say who they are — there is no name to look up. Open a face's photo to see who it is, then put a name against that number and every card and sensor uses it. Clear a box to remove a name.

{faces}

A face has no photo link until its recording has downloaded.

layout.description:
Give each camera a number for how close it is to your door: **0 for the one nearest the street**, higher as they get closer to the entrance. A gate camera might be 0 and the doorbell 1.

This is the one thing the integration cannot work out on its own — the hub reports no geometry. With it, a recognised person moving from one camera to another reads as *approaching* or *leaving* rather than just a list of places.

Leave every camera on the same number to turn this off; no direction is reported unless it is genuinely known.{suggestion}
